            "review_title": "Review at Restaurant Three Sister's",
            "review_text": "Amanda E\nAntwerp, Belgium47 contributions\n0\nDown a little alley\nJun 2013 • Friends\nA lot of restaurants serve international food and our focused on Russian tourists. Sometimes even the menu is written in Russian. 3 Sister's is different. Is a really small, cheap restaurant down a little alley. It's more quite than the main street of Nha Trang. We paid 10.000 VND for a Saigon beer. We ordered some morning glory, roasted fish and tradional spring rolls. The food was fresh and tasty. The also offer some cocktails, but that was pretty new. Compared to the rest of our meal, they where quit expensive. You should try the banana fritters as a dessert. They're delicious!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten July 17, 2013",
            "rating": 5.0,
